<title>CHILE: Escondida gold output up sharply in 1996.</title>
<headline>Escondida gold output up sharply in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Escondida's gold production rose last year to 187,268 ounces contained in concentrates from 106,268 ounces in 1995, Minera Escondida Ltda reported.</p>
<p>In December, gold output was 14,941 ounces. Comparative figures for December 1995 were not available.</p>
<p>The mine is owned by Broken Hill Proprietary and RTZ Corp Plc.</p>
<p>((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
